2026-11-05: v0.1.8 released (43e6cbc; #29 merged as df228a4, release prep #30). Wheel sha256 df5cf859…, SHA256SUMS verified. It fixes BenchBox's hosted-review defects in v0.1.7 (PR #3959):
- the old surface comes from base workflows only;
- step-level references are handled, and in the end every Theseus action and every step-level `./` reference holds (Theseus supports only job-level reusable workflows plus its package);
- references must equal the lock pin;
- audit-coverage exits 2 on staging failure;
- gitdiff has a runner seam.
It also fixes the empty model catalog, which affected both hosted and local review: the isolated listing uses a placeholder credential, guarded by candidate row 13. Overhead is now per mode (inline 80K, file-list and promotion 170K, from archived p95 + 10%). Unknown capacity is never assumed. The independent review took 4 rounds before SHIP.
